nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In general, you would like a better suit to overcall at the 2 level, either a 6-card suit or 3 honors. But, as East, I love bidding 2@C over 1@D as it makes it hard for us to find our fit. So I would bid 2@C also even though the club suit is not ideal. It is worth the risk to interfere.|
PG| ***** 2 ***** |


mb|D|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Had partner opened 1@C, I would like my hand much more. I love 5-4-4-0 distribution in general, but having a void in partner's suit is a huge minus.|
PG| ***** 3 ***** |


mb|P|mb|2S|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|We do have a 9-card fit. We could be missing game. Partner did not jump so he can not be that strong. So, I am going to make a conservative pass. This illustrates how your hand gets stronger or weaker as the auction progresses.|
PG| ***** 4 ***** |


