mb|3C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|A perfect 3@C bid. In fact, sometimes at what is termed "favorable vulnerability" meaning you are not vulnerable and they are you should actually preempt one higher than normal.|
PG| ***** 22 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So, particularly because of the void, 4@C is possible, but I think 3@C is better because the club suit, although reasonable, is not great. With better clubs (say 3 honors) I very well might open 4@C with that distribution.|
PG| ***** 23 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BEast: ^*NWhat about being vulnerable?|
PG| ***** 24 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I would open 3@C even if vulnerable. I usually make the same preempt vulnerable or not unless I have a very marginal preempt.|
PG| ***** 25 ***** |


