UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Very nicely played. The suit combination of 3 or 4 small opposite QJx, which is what East had in hearts is a good one to memorize. 75% of the time that will yield one trick so long as you can lead towards your QJ twice. Basically if North held one or both heart honors (75%) East will score one heart trick.|
PG| ***** 37 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The only time it does not is if South held both the @HA and @HK.|
PG| ***** 38 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Further, North did well to pass. You hate to let them play the hand when they preempt. The @CQ is not worth much so North really only has 10 working HCP. If the @CQ were say the @SQ, then I might reopen with a double. You have to reevaluate your hand based on the auction.|
PG| ***** 39 ***** |


