qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   July 10, 2024|pn|hondo717,vs_bbo,aspiring,Hi Its Me|
md|1SAQ9HA87D832CJ842,S6HQ62DT74CAKQT63,SK8742HKT94DAQ9C9,SJT53HJ53DKJ65C75|sv|e|
mb|P|mb|1C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West has a clear 1@C opener. I use the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| to decide whether or not to open. West has 11 HCP and 9 cards in clubs/hearts for 20 meaning it is an opening hand.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 41 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In fact, I suggest you use Bergen Hand Evaluation to decide how many points your hand has. Doing so, then West adds an extra point for his quality 3 honor club suit making the hand actually worth 12 points.|
PG| ***** 42 ***** |


mb|1S|mb|P|MB|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|My hand is ostensibly worth 11 HCP with some minuses. The @CJ is somewhat dubious given the 1@C opener and I dislike 4-3-3-3 distribution. However, I do have a 3-card limit raise. So I should make a cue bid of 2@C to show I have 10 points and at least 3 spades. I prefer to have 4 but @SAQx is good enough that I still should make a limit raise.|
PG| ***** 43 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Please note that 2@S shows 6-9 and 3@S shows less than a limit raise with 4 spades even if you don't play |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenraises,Bergen Raises^*N|CP||FP||AT|. In general (where a jump to 3@S always shows a weak hand, not a limit raise): and play that 3@S over an opening 1@S shows a limit raise. However, you definitely should not play that in competition. You should play 3@S is weak and a cue bid is how you show a limit raise.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


mb|2C|an|a limit raise|
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If I were not vulnerable, I would bid 3@C over 2@C with West hand. But pass is fine.|
PG| ***** 46 ***** |


mb|4S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Let us count North's |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=declarerpoints,Bergen Declarer Points^*N|CP||FP||at| to see why she bid 4@S. North has a very good 12 HCP with 2.5 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=quicktricks,Quick Trick^*N|CP||FP||at|, 1 length point. 13 is North's |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at|. Once we find a fit, North has 2 points for the singleton declarer add ons. A singleton in opener's suit is particularly useful.|
PG| ***** 47 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Finally, North can add 1 point for the 4 card side heart suit for 16 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=declarerpoints,Bergen Declarer Points^*N|CP||FP||at|. So, N/S have 26 combined points at least enough for game. But since I have rather a weak limit raise, this is a very iffy game.|
PG| ***** 48 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Again it is showing that the auction helps determine how you revalue your hand.|
PG| ***** 49 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
