qx|A6|st||rh||ah|Board 6 IMPs   -   July 10, 2024|pn|hondo717,vs_bbo,Hi Its Me,aspiring|
md|4SAJ9732H962D4C642,SKQ65HQTDA93CAT85,S84HK743DJT87CK97,STHAJ85DKQ652CQJ3|sv|e|
mb|1D|mb|2S?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West has a really nice hand and slam is possible although not that likely and West is hand cuffed to explore because of preempt by South. That is the main idea behind preempts to take up valuable bidding space making the opponents auctions more difficult. So you have to make your best guess.|
PG| ***** 108 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Further, sometimes after a preempt you need to consider another bidding principle that is ^*BGame Before Slam^*n. That mean you optimize your bidding for games and don't worry if you occasionally miss a slam. Therefore, for all those reasons, West should bid 3N and that is likely to be their best spot.|
PG| ***** 109 ***** |


mb|3N|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
