sk|s|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|S8|pc|ST?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now you may ask what should I play? I know based on the lead, @S8, that North's most likely holding is 8-x (because with a singleton 8 that would give West 5 spades, possible but not as likely). And I know North does not have the @SK or @SQ. So if I play the @SA I set up two tricks right away for declarer.|
